Subject: shards-api, shards-ipc: an image run takes shares another server serves (D286, image channel 52)
Why: kiln's microVM engine shares each agent's slates volume into its guest over slates' own virtio-fs device, a stream handed to Shards with no host mount between (kiln goal 01a1ec34599974448f6b7663ddb07001); upstream on Shards' branch agents/g265-kiln-shards-microvm-served-image-share (4ff40fc99 and 5376b406a on main 4776b2e56; e4e0118c8 and 74d1bc82f on this revision), which ROOT lands after Shards' v0.8.0 tag; dropped once Hex takes a Shards revision that holds it

